{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KurecSHcEEDZJ1Hp2F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft, a few questions. Your answers will change what the summary says, so it's worth sorting them out first.\n\n1. **Where does the rest of the salary come from?** The attorney costs $78,000 a year and the foundation's cap is $45,000, so each year there's a $33,000 gap ($66,000 over the two years). Reviewers will check for this first. Is the gap covered by the county contract, another grant, or your general budget? Is that money committed or still pending?\n\n2. **How does the June departure fit in?** If one of your two attorneys leaves in June, does this grant pay for a third attorney, or would you really be replacing the one who left and staying at two? Are you already funded to replace them? If not, the honest framing may be \"keep two attorneys and add one,\" and the summary has to make that clear.\n\n3. **What's the risk with the October county renewal?** Do you expect the $60,000 to be renewed, and does any of it go toward this position? If the funder learns later that the match depended on a contract that lapsed, that hurts you more than saying so now.\n\n4. **What can you commit to?** For example: a hire date, how many extra tenants a year the new attorney would represent (around 80?), and whether you'll start tracking outcomes for tenants you turn away so you finally have a comparison for your 58%.\n\n5. **What can you show about your track record and the funder's priorities?** How long the clinic has been running, any past foundation grants and how they went, and any language the foundation uses in its call for proposals (e.g., \"access to justice,\" \"rural,\" \"housing stability\") that I should echo.\n\n6. **Is there anything else a reviewer might know or find out?** Any staff turnover, a missed grant deliverable, a competing clinic in the county, or an issue with how the 58% was counted?\n\nIf you don't know some of these, just say so and I'll write without them rather than guess."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":781,"cache_read_input_tokens":9572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":781},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1786379c-6a2e-4c7c-bba5-0119c4b0cdb2","uuid":"45a6881a-ac01-4f0d-9634-4a3ca80e77ab","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:36:03.384Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7KurUhmDLNPRCiwmTLS"}
