{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KwCu3fqjJikL5Wfstj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the summary using only what you gave me.\n\n<final_document>\n**Project Summary: Tenant Defense Project**\n\nThe Tenant Defense Project requests $90,000 over two years ($45,000 a year) to hire a third staff attorney to represent tenants facing eviction.\n\n**Need.** Last year 1,140 eviction cases were filed in our county. With two attorneys, we represented the tenant in 163 of them, about one in seven. We turned away roughly 300 more tenants because no attorney was free to take their case. Each of our attorneys carries about 80 open cases.\n\n**Results.** In the cases we handled, 58% ended with the tenant staying in the home or getting at least 60 days to move. We do not yet have a comparable figure for tenants without a lawyer in our county. Starting in January, we will request court-wide outcome data from the county clerk so that our results can be measured against that baseline.\n\n**Project.** The new attorney will take cases from tenants we now have to turn away. One of our current attorneys leaves in June and has agreed to spend her last month training the new hire.\n\n**Budget.** The position costs $78,000 a year with benefits, or $156,000 over two years. This grant would cover $90,000. A family fund has pledged $20,000 a year for both years, and we will cover the remaining $13,000 a year from our general budget. Separately, our $60,000 annual county contract is up for renewal in October, and renewal is not yet certain.\n\n**Accountability.** Every six months we will report to the foundation the number of cases opened and how each one ended.\n</final_document>\n\nIt's about 255 words. A few things to settle before March 3:\n\n- **Will you have three attorneys or two?** A reviewer will read \"third attorney\" and \"one leaves in June\" together and ask this. If you find out you're funded to replace her separately, add a sentence saying so. That's the strongest fix available. If you aren't funded to replace her, the summary is still accurate, but you should decide whether to call the position a \"third attorney.\"\n- **The training handoff may not happen.** The foundation decides in May, she leaves in June, and your last opening took five months to fill. Unless you start recruiting before the award, the new hire probably won't arrive in time for her last month. If that's likely, change the sentence to something like \"will document her caseload and procedures for the new hire\" so you don't promise an overlap you can't deliver.\n- **The county contract line is optional.** I included it because a reviewer may know about it, and it's better they hear it from you. The position doesn't depend on that money, so you could cut the line if the foundation doesn't ask about overall organizational funding.\n- **Add anything that shows your track record.** If you find any (years in operation, past grants completed, any recognition), one sentence of it would help. The draft currently has nothing on this."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1049,"cache_read_input_tokens":10353,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1049},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1786379c-6a2e-4c7c-bba5-0119c4b0cdb2","uuid":"5752a1c9-80ed-4356-bc17-f69c34d3dd7b","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:36:42.107Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7KwCgf19278wUeWQAWT"}
